    "created_at": "2016-05-20T02:52:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T02:52:21Z",
    "body": "Oh, dang, this is a definite spec hole.\n\nI think we have to somehow define implicit pass-through constructors for all HTML element classes (including abstract base classes like HTMLMediaElement).\n\nAdvice from other editors on the best way to do this would be appreciated. Right now, per IDL, this will always fail. I guess we could add a new extended attribute to IDL, [PassThroughConstructor]? That seems most feasible to me at the moment.\n",
