    "created_at": "2016-05-20T13:11:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T13:12:27Z",
    "body": "I have an even better idea. Why don't we patch Web IDL to say that any derived class constructor is automatically a pass-through constructor. That will solve this problem in general: any time someone uses IDL to define a base class that is subclassable, all derived classes are also subclassable.\n\nI will work on a Web IDL PR soon. It will require updating Web IDL's definition of class constructors to modern ES (e.g. using [[Construct]] instead of [[Call]], NewTarget, etc.).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
